Statistical reform


in the United Kingdom and Uganda has attempted to


answer this difﬁcult question and emerged with differ-


ing administrative models and they constitute a unique


form in contradistinction to what hitherto countries are


generally accustomed to. It appears that the study of


statistics as a source of independent source of evidence


locates such institutions in the realm of constitutional


